WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.198
This is Meera.

2
00:00:02.218 --> 00:00:04.961
She designs for a living — on her Mac.

3
00:00:04.981 --> 00:00:08.480
But the rest of her life lives on her phone.

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.350
The new Orbit brings them together.

5
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.646
Open Orbit, and her phone is right there.

6
00:00:17.666 --> 00:00:22.230
Her wallpaper, her messages, what's playing — and who called.

7
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.170
When her mum calls, Meera answers on her Mac — and talks right through it.

8
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.653
It takes a one-minute setup on the phone, just once.

9
00:00:37.673 --> 00:00:39.760
Orbit even pairs itself.

10
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.465
Texts, WhatsApp, every contact — in one place.

11
00:00:45.485 --> 00:00:49.230
She replies without reaching for her phone.

12
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.957
The video she started on the bus?

13
00:00:53.977 --> 00:00:59.390
One drag into her browser, and it carries on — at the very same second.

14
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.190
And the apps that only live on her phone open right on her Mac.

15
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:16.140
When she heads out, the page she was reading is already waiting, at the top of her phone.

16
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:22.350
All of it, in a menu bar that feels like it came with her Mac.

17
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.850
Orbit. Your Android, at home on your Mac.

